{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794647277,"nonce":"xjJyoB8Lm9nLJpp3JwvHEkh819U=","message":"`hxn build hl --target \u003ctriple\u003e` and `hxn package hl --target \u003ctriple\u003e` now build the HashLink adapter as a staticlib and copy it to `lib\u003clibrary\u003e.a`; `hxn.Bind` copies that archive next to `main.hl` when compiling with `-D hxn_triple=\u003ctriple\u003e`. `tests/mobile/run.sh ios-sim|android hl` packages each example that way and has Ash link it with `--native-lib`.\n\nRun with ash 1a6ff690 and its runtimes built from source into `target/release/\u003ctriple\u003e/`: all seven examples pass on the Pixel_9_Pro emulator (`aarch64-linux-android`) and in the iOS simulator (`aarch64-apple-ios-sim`). The hxcpp mode of tests/mobile still passes on both; tests/cli and tests/examples pass on Ash (hybrid), hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm and Emscripten. Not run: Ash jit/interp modes for the host suites, stock HashLink on the NUC, Windows.\n\nNot in CI: Ash has no tagged release that bundles the mobile runtimes yet, so a CI job would have to build them from source. Left for when Ash cuts one.","files":null}]}